al Students Apply For Financial Aid Alternate Resources Federal & Campus Work Study Loans and Loan Info Outside Scholarships Scholarships and Grants Scholarships & Grants – Online Year-Round Pell Grants Military Aid Military Scholarships Consumer Right to Know: Policies and Information Verification Student Financial Forms Averett Online Financial Aid Forms Financial Aid Calculators NetPrice Calculator Net Price Calculator (Averett Online) ABSN Early Aid Estimator Student Health Insurance Student Accounts – Traditional Student Accounts – Averett Online GradReady Level Up Virginia Contact Us Student Life About Student Life Arrival and Departure Policy Averett Bookstore Campus Mailroom Public Safety Disaster Preparedness Emergency Procedures Winter Weather Preparedness Tornado Evacuation Locations Fire Procedure Counseling Services Counseling – Schedule an Appointment Counseling FAQ What to Expect from Counseling Services Mental Health Emergencies Telehealth Information Dean of Students’ Office Families & Parents International Student Services Transportation Dining Hall / Jut’s Café Faculty & Staff Meals Residence Life Forms Health Services Fever/COVID/Flu Information Required Health Forms Student Health Insurance Housing and Residence Life Maintenance Request Housing and Residence Life Forms Returning Student Housing Incoming Student Housing Residence Halls Bishop Residence Hall Fugate Residence Hall Main Residence Hall Danville Residence Hall Averett Commons Apartments RA Selection Timeline Residency Requirement Spiritual Life Student Engagement Clubs and Organizations Commuter Students Intramural Sports Orientation SGA Student Handbook Athletics Alumni Homecoming Upcoming Alumni Events Alumni Board Alumni Board Application Alumni Association Alumni Awards Alumni Awards Nomination Distinguished Alumni Award Recipients Mary Jo Davis Outstanding Alumni Award Recipients Recent Distinguished Alumni Award Recipients Frank Campbell Service Award Recipients Fugate-Davis Women’s Leadership Award Recipients Alumni News Contact Info Update Refer a Friend Request a Transcript Give to Averett Merchandise Giving Ways to Give Donate to the Averett Fund Donate to Cougar Cares Join the Circle of Champions Barbara Kushubar ’75 Memorial Fund Charles S. Harris Memorial Fund Giving Tips Planned Giving Contact Us Donate Now MENU Please Select Page --- Office of the President Averett Blog Averett at a Glance Mission, Vision, & Core Values Human Resources & Payroll Employment Opportunities Traditional Faculty Employment Opportunities Averett Online Faculty Employment Opportunities Staff Employment Opportunities Working at Averett Employee Benefits & Wellness Payroll Information Title IX Our Campuses Media News & Events Find AU People Arts@Averett Home ‣ About Us ‣ Employment Opportunities ‣ Averett Online Faculty Employment Opportunities AVERETT ONLINE ADJUNCT FACULTY POOL The Averett Online program maintains a pool of qualified adjunct instructors to teach online or at ground locations.  Most online courses run 5 – 8 weeks for undergraduate-level programs and 2 – 6 weeks for graduate-level programs. Most courses are pre-developed to allow instructors to focus on student learning and engagement. Required Qualifications to teach at the Bachelor degree level, are a minimum of a Master’s degree and 18 or more graduate-level credit hours in the discipline to be taught and relevant professional or teaching experience. Teaching at the graduate level requires a terminal degree and 18 or more graduate-level credit hours in the discipline to be taught. At this time, we are not recruiting for specific positions; however if you meet the qualification standards and have an interest in being considered to join the adjunct instructor pool, please complete and submit the Faculty Interest Form .  Specific questions may be sent to: [email protected] . Programs Offered through the Averett Online program are designed for working adults seeking to advance their current careers, be promoted, or change careers.  Degree programs include: Bachelor Degree Bachelor of Business Administration Bachelor of Arts/Bachelor of Science Management Science Computer Information Systems Criminal Justice Sociology Bachelor of Science in Sociology and Criminal Justice Bachelor of Science in Nursing (ABSN) Graduate Degrees Master of Business Administration Master of Business Administration with Concentration in Human Resource Management Concentration in Leadership Concentration in Marketing Master of Education Curriculum and Instruction Special Education (licensure) and endorsement track Administration and Supervision (licensure) endorsement Math Specialist Elementary Education Special Education (pk-6, 6-8, and 6-12) graduate certificate Reading Specialist, Gifted graduate certificate Administration and Supervision graduate certificate To learn more please visit our Averett Online website . Please note: Background checks are required for all positions. An applicant must have an unrestricted right to work in the U.S. Averett University’s Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, can be found at https://www.averett.edu/clery . Averett University’s policies, programs and activities, including hiring practices, comply with federal and state laws and regulations prohibiting discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, sex, disability, sexual orientation, and gender identity or expression and veteran status. Inquiries related to the University’s compliance with Title IX should be directed to Averett’s Title IX Coordinator at [email protected] . Additional contact information, reporting options, and the University’s Title IX Sexual Harassment Policy can be found at https://www.averett.edu/about-us/title-ix/ . Inquiries may be made externally to the Department of Education’s Office for Civil Rights: https://www.ed.gov/ocr . Averett University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and an Employer of National Service. AmeriCorps, Peace Corps, and other national service alumni are encouraged to apply. MAIN CAMPUS 420 West Main St., Danville, VA 24541 Phone: (434) 791-5600 1-800-AVERETT NORTH CAMPUS 707 Mount Cross Road, Danville, VA 24540 Phone: (434) 791-5700 1-800-AVERETT © 2026 Averett University. All rights reserved. Careers | Sitemap | Privacy & Cookies Policy We use cookies on our website to give you the most relevant experience by remembering your preferences and repeat visits. By clicking “Accept”, you consent to the use of ALL the cookies. Do not sell my personal information . Settings Accept Privacy & Cookies Policy Close Privacy Overview This website uses cookies to improve your experience while you navigate through the website. Out of these cookies, the cookies that are categorized as necessary are stored on your browser as they are as essential for the working of basic functionalities of the website. We also use third-party cookies that help us analyze and understand how you use this website. These cookies will be stored in your browser only with your consent. You also have the option to opt-out of these cookies. But opting out of some of these cookies may have an effect on your browsing experience. Necessary Necessary Always Enabled Necessary cookies are absolutely essential for the website to function properly. This category only includes cookies that ensures basic functionalities and security features of the website. These cookies do not store any personal information. SAVE & ACCEPT"
